  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The word \"every\" indicates that we use a universal quantifier, $∀.$\n\n- The words \"there exists\" indicate that we use an existential quantifier, $∃.$\n\n- The sentence refers to rational numbers. So, by denoting our numbers as $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n∀\\,a\\in Q,\\,∃\\,b\\in Q.\n$$\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as follows:\n\n$$\na+b=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows:\n\n$∀\\,a\\in Q,\\,∃\\,b\\in Q,\\,a+b=0$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
